### v1.0.6 — Architecture Innovations & Enterprise Hardening

- [x] **[IDE-106-01] State-Aware Checkpoint & Resume Engine**: Implemented dynamic statefile tracking (`.z2z_checkpoint.db` / TSV) recording `DONE`, `FAILED`, `MISSING` states per account to allow interrupted batch migrations to resume without re-exporting completed mailboxes (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-02] Parallel Mailbox Multi-Worker Orchestrator**: Added configurable concurrent worker pool (`CONCURRENCY=4..16`) for `script_export_FULL.sh` and `script_import_FULL.sh` with CPU/RAM load throttling (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-03] Secure Credential Passing via Temporary File Descriptor**: Replaced `-w "${ldap_auth_token}"` CLI password arguments in `ldapsearch`, `ldapadd`, and `ldapdelete` with `-y <secure_file>` (permissions `0600` in `/dev/shm` cleaned via trap) to eliminate process table (`ps aux`) credential exposure (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-04] Incremental Delta Mailbox Synchronization**: Created `util/sync_delta_mailbox.sh` utilizing timestamp REST query filtering (`getRestURL "//?fmt=tgz&query=after:\"YYYY/MM/DD\""`) to sync only new incoming mail during cutover windows (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-05] Pre-Flight Disk Capacity & Inode Safety Guard**: Implemented `check_disk_capacity()` calculating total mailbox storage against destination mount point free space (`df -Pk`) with a safety threshold buffer (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-07] Base64 Encoding Guard for Sieve & Out-of-Office Payloads**: Stored multi-line vacation replies and complex Sieve filter scripts in Base64 encoding during staging to guarantee character and newline integrity during SOAP/zmprov injection (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-08] Post-Migration Data Integrity Verifier**: Created `util/verify_migration.sh` to compare source vs destination account lists, mailbox sizes, and folder counts with a color-coded delta reconciliation report (`MATCH`, `DELTA_WARN`, `MISSING`) (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-09] Safe Admin Import Verification Guard**: Added strict validation in `skell/importar_ldap.sh` checking `CONTAS.ldif` for a valid replacement `uid=admin` record before allowing `ldapdelete` on the target server to prevent accidental admin lockout (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-12] Direct Remote SSH/Rsync Streaming Pipeline**: Created `util/stream_mailbox_direct.sh` to pipe `zmmailbox getRestURL` output directly over an SSH tunnel into the target server's `postRestURL` without requiring intermediate local disk staging (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-14] Automatic Mail Routing Cutover & Maintenance Freeze Mode**: Created `util/freeze_source_accounts.sh` to set source accounts to `maintenance` mode (`zimbraAccountStatus maintenance`) and redirect Postfix transport maps to the new server during DNS propagation (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-15] Generic IMAP to Zimbra Imapsync Ingestion Wrapper**: Created `util/imapsync_wrapper.sh` providing structured, multi-threaded IMAP migration for importing non-Zimbra mail servers (cPanel, Postfix/Dovecot, Exchange, Google Workspace) directly into Zimbra (v1.0.6)
- [x] **[IDE-106-16] Executive Post-Migration HTML Summary Report**: Created `util/generate_migration_report.sh` producing an interactive, self-contained HTML report with storage graphs, domain breakdowns, and success/failure statistics (v1.0.6)
- [x] **PID File Locking Mechanism**: Added `flock` locking in `z2z.sh` to prevent simultaneous conflicting migration runs (v1.0.6)

